Business Requirements Document (BRD)
Project Name
Indom – Student Project Marketplace Platform
Version
1.0
Author
Nikish Bastola
Date
June 2026

1. Executive Summary
Indom is a web-based platform designed to connect students with startups, organizations, research labs, and university departments through short-term project opportunities.
The platform addresses the gap between students seeking practical experience and organizations seeking motivated talent for project-based work. Indom enables organizations to post projects, review applicants, and manage project workflows while allowing students to discover opportunities and gain real-world experience.

2. Business Problem
Students often graduate with limited practical experience despite completing academic coursework.
At the same time, startups, research groups, and organizations frequently require support for short-term initiatives but lack an efficient way to identify and engage qualified student talent.
Current methods such as email outreach, spreadsheets, and informal networking are inefficient, difficult to scale, and lack transparency.
A centralized platform is needed to streamline project discovery, application management, and collaboration between students and organizations.

3. Business Objectives
The primary objectives of Indom are:
1.	Increase student access to experiential learning opportunities.
2.	Reduce the effort required for organizations to recruit student contributors.
3.	Create a centralized marketplace for project-based collaboration.
4.	Improve visibility into application and project workflows.
5.	Enable data-driven decision-making through analytics and reporting.

4. Stakeholders
Primary Stakeholders
Students
Individuals seeking project-based learning opportunities.
Organizations
Companies, startups, university departments, and research groups posting projects.
Research Labs
Faculty-led teams seeking student contributors.
Indom Administrators
Platform administrators responsible for governance and maintenance.

Secondary Stakeholders
Universities
Institutions interested in increasing student engagement and employability.
Faculty Members
Professors seeking students for research and innovation initiatives.

5. Scope
In Scope
•	Student registration and authentication
•	Organization registration and authentication
•	Project posting and management
•	Student project browsing
•	Project applications
•	Applicant review workflows
•	Application status tracking
•	Analytics dashboard
•	CSV reporting and export functionality
Out of Scope
•	Payroll processing
•	Financial transactions
•	Background checks
•	Real-time messaging
•	Mobile application support

6. Functional Requirements
FR-01 User Authentication
The system shall allow users to register and log in securely.
Acceptance Criteria
•	Users can create accounts.
•	Users can log in.
•	Users can log out.

FR-02 Role Management
The system shall support the following roles:
•	Student
•	Organization
•	Administrator
Acceptance Criteria
•	Each user is assigned a role.
•	Users access role-specific functionality.

FR-03 Project Posting
Organizations shall be able to create and manage project listings.
Acceptance Criteria
•	Create project
•	Edit project
•	View project
•	Archive project

FR-04 Project Applications
Students shall be able to apply for projects.
Acceptance Criteria
•	Submit application
•	Attach project interest message
•	Track application status

FR-05 Applicant Workflow Management
Organizations shall manage applicants through a structured workflow.
Workflow States
•	Applied
•	Under Review
•	Interviewing
•	Accepted
•	Rejected
•	Completed
Acceptance Criteria
•	Status updates are saved.
•	Workflow history is visible.

FR-06 Analytics Dashboard
Organizations shall access project and applicant analytics.
KPIs
•	Total Projects
•	Total Applications
•	Pending Applications
•	Accepted Applications
•	Acceptance Rate
•	Top Requested Skills

FR-07 Reporting
Organizations shall export applicant data.
Acceptance Criteria
•	CSV export available
•	Applicant details included
•	Status information included

7. Non-Functional Requirements
Security
•	User authentication required
•	Role-based access controls enforced
•	Secure database access through Supabase RLS policies
Performance
•	Dashboard pages load within 3 seconds under normal usage
Availability
•	Platform available 99% of the time during operational periods
Scalability
•	Platform supports growth in users, projects, and applications without redesign

8. Success Metrics
The success of Indom will be measured using the following KPIs:
Metric	Description
Projects Posted	Total number of active projects
Applications Submitted	Total applications received
Acceptance Rate	Accepted applications / Total applications
Project Completion Rate	Completed projects / Total projects
Active Organizations	Number of participating organizations
Active Students	Number of engaged students

9. Risks
Risk	                                                              Impact
Low organization adoption	                                        Reduced project availability
Low student engagement	                                            Reduced platform value
Data quality issues	                                                Inaccurate analytics
Scalability limitations	                                            Performance degradation

10. Future Enhancements
•	AI-powered project recommendations
•	Resume matching and skill analysis
•	Automated applicant ranking
•	Integrated messaging system
•	Mobile application
•	Advanced analytics and forecasting


